{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats","id":1033613,"title":"Best and worst fighting styles for supernatural splats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-17T13:46:28-08:00","id":1033613,"title":"Best and worst fighting styles for supernatural splats","content":"Despite my fascination for the Adamantine Arrows, an area of the CoD system where I have poor or mediocre grasp is the various Fighting Styles and their relative merits. So I would inquire about the forum's collective wisdom concerning which styles look especially appropriate or of little utility for combat-focused characters of the various supernatural splats. I'm especially interested in unarmed combat and melee weapon styles, and about vampires, mages, beasts, changelings, geists, and psychics. Besides the CoD stuff, please include the styles to be found in Hurt Locker and individual game lines in your analysis if you are familiar with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-17-2017, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:59:27-08:00","id":1033622,"title":"","content":"Any of the grappling styles can do nasty things when paired with the ability of several werewolf forms to start a grapple when initiating a normal attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T14:11:07-08:00","id":1033633,"title":"","content":"It would be super cool to see some new fighting styles for Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T14:32:24-08:00","id":1033653,"title":"","content":"Kindred Dueling and Ride the Wave are both very good for vampires, though in different ways.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has Relentless Assault and Tactical Shifting, also both very good for werewolves. Relentless Assault was so good Beasts stole it.<br /> <br /> First edition's werewolf had the Slow Kill, which was a fantastic grappling fighting style. Once you've reached the fourth dot, any other grappling fighting style would make you a severely dangerous grappler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-17-2017, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:26:51-08:00","id":1033685,"title":"","content":"A Mage with Time 3 and Defensive Fighting (Armed) can get a Dodge pool upwards of 40 dice, then convert it into counter attacks against anyone who attacks them. Which is pretty ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:42:00-08:00","id":1033690,"title":"","content":"Not really ridiculous. Other mages don't really care about his dice/combat capabilities when they can just order him to shoot himself in the head (Mind 2), shield themselves from all physical damage (Forces 2), teleport him into the volcano (Space 3), make his clothes into his personal coffin (Matter 3) and so on and on. It is possible that mages don't have more fighting styles because they don't need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T16:09:17-08:00","id":1033708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1033690#post1033690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really ridiculous. Other mages don't really care about his dice/combat capabilities when they can just order him to shoot himself in the head (Mind 2), shield themselves from all physical damage (Forces 2), teleport him into the volcano (Space 3), make his clothes into his personal coffin (Matter 3) and so on and on. It is possible that mages don't have more fighting styles because they don't need to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, but this thread is about good splat + style combos, plus sometimes you just want to dish out some good old fashioned melee hurt.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Another fine combo for any Vampire with Celerity, or Werewolf with Hit and Run would be Light Weapons. In single combat you can throw all your defense into Thrust, then use Celerity/Hit and Run to avoid the counter attack. Added fun if you feint the turn before for extra dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-17-2017, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T16:43:24-08:00","id":1033725,"title":"","content":"Yea, sometimes you want. I'm saying it in the spirit of this thread, I think. Where the purpose of fighting styles for mortal, vampire or woof is to make them more deadly and efficient, for a mage it is redundant, optional and not so important. <br /> I'll add something to the thread even so. Heavy Weapons Warding Stance can give you some nice armor (like 10+) when combined with eg baseball bat perfected by Mankey Paw (Fate 3) or similar Matter 3 spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T16:48:34-08:00","id":1033730,"title":"","content":"I really enjoy Psychokinetic Combat from hurt locker, generate an element aura, armor piecing and ignore cover, cause explosions as a reflexive action, and regain willpower when you deal damage. Although I have to say, I'm not a big fan of the fourth level effect. Adding damage to your next attack equal to the amount of lethal you take seems suicidal. Although I suppose I can see using that when the enemy I'm fighting is likely to kill me in one blow, It doesn't matter how hurt I am if I could take them out first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12860-your3rdshadow","name":"Your3rdShadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:33:00-08:00","id":1033758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1033725#post1033725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, sometimes you want. I'm saying it in the spirit of this thread, I think. Where the purpose of fighting styles for mortal, vampire or woof is to make them more deadly and efficient, for a mage it is redundant, optional and not so important.<br /> I'll add something to the thread even so. Heavy Weapons Warding Stance can give you some nice armor (like 10+) when combined with eg baseball bat perfected by Mankey Paw (Fate 3) or similar Matter 3 spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue against that redundancy, as would the Adamant Arrow. But, rather than argue, let me instead point out that Mages are in the interesting position where they can grant powers to others. So even if the Mage herself had no use for Defensive Combat, she could just as easily Accelerate someone else. Same goes with your excellent Perfected Baseball Bat example.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T05:33:47-08:00","id":1033967,"title":"","content":"I see various worthwhile suggestions and I'm thankful for them. What about other fighting styles, such as Boxing, Improvised Weaponry, Martial Arts, Sistema, Street Fighting, and Unarmed Defense ? Are they sufficiently good to be noteworthy for any splat ? And although they may not be, technically speaking, styles, there are other specialized fighting Merits for some splats, such as Adamant Hand for Arrow mages, Killer Instinct for beasts, and Rites of the Impaled for Ordo vampires that seem to belong in the grey zone between true fighting styles and combat-worthy supernatural powers (Arcana, Disciplines, Atavisms, Contracts, etc). What's your opinion of them ? Is Parkour any good at all for anyone ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-18-2017, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:11:02-08:00","id":1034050,"title":"","content":"Killer Instinct is a very powerful combat merit. It's great for snipers and it's versatile enough to help significantly against both armored and high defense enemies in melee range. <br /> <br /> With the advent of Hurt Locker the question is less about whether a style as a whole is good and more whether individual maneuvers are useful and tagged in a way they can be chained together. Most styles have at least one or two good dots, most also have a couple that are too situational or of marginal utility. It really depends on what you're going for. There are some notable combos. Clinch Strike is useful for almost everybody who isn't a werewolf but wants to grapple. Trained Bite is a really cheap upgrade for werewolves, vamps, and gristlegrinders. Strength performance 4 meshes really well with grappling styles, essentially giving you a free success to your pool most rolls.<br /> <br /> Changelings are very well suited to take advantage of high Dex builds with the Might of the Terrible Brute Beast Affinity, which adds Wyrd to Dex instead of Strength. There are a lot of merits that can synergize with high Dex. Court of the West's five dot Mantle lets you use the higher of Wits or Dex to calculate defense, and if that's not available to your character the first dot of Street Fighting will do the same thing at the cost of -1 on your attack roll. Armed Defense and Light Weapons both make very good use of high defense pools, and can easily be hybridized under style tag rules. AD1/LW2/AD3 is a really good 3 dot style. On the unarmed side of things, Boxing is a very solid style with two dots that really shine on a high dex character. Defensive jab punishes every failed attack. It's not ultra strong, but it's a nice bonus, particularly since it allows you to dodge to victory. Combination blows is okay in mortal hands, but given to a Changeling with MotTB it can quickly turn into Fist of the North Star. <br /> <br /> Also, if you're using the Beast optional rule that opens Advanced merits to other supernaturals Advanced Double Jointed + MotTB can let a Changeling out grapple nearly anybody.<br /> <br /> Still, in terms of sheer dice the winner has to be a Skitterskulk with 5 dots of West Mantle, Armed Defense, and a Blood Pennon. The necessary fighting styles and Mantle can be had at character creation, the pennon for an extra 5 exp. Assuming max Dex and Weaponry that's a base dodge of 30 dice, double to 60 with the pennon, and that's at Wyrd 1 without even using contracts. <br /> <br /> As others have mentioned, Relentless Assault is a great style. By itself it gives some decent bonuses, but what really sells it for me is how easily those abilities mesh with many other melee styles. High defense styles can use it one on one, since it retains defense against a single target. High armor styles benefit from another dot. Everybody can use a -1 die +1 damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:22:50-08:00","id":1036928,"title":"","content":"I've noticed that the the rules for Light Weapons don't require you to be rolling on Weaponry so for 7 merit dots (Street Fighting 2, Shive 2, Light Weapons 2 and Martal Arts 1) you can roll Brawl plus your Defence -2 to stake a vampire.<br /> A strict reading of the rules (but no sane ST) would also allow you to use both Flurry and Whirlwind Strike at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":".  Correcting rules. See post below. 01-24-2017, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:59:49-08:00","id":1036951,"title":"","content":"Should be -2, although the attribute prereqs make that a hefty investment just to be able to trade brawl for weaponry on the roll.<br /> <br /> It does make me wonder what the roll to just rip out a heart with your bare hands would be. It doesn't seem terribly feasible in real life, but Martial Arts 5 lets your bare hands deal as much damage as machetes, and much more than stakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:25:40-08:00","id":1036962,"title":"","content":"Yeah, at that level of training and skill you should be able to stake vampires if you try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:06:41-08:00","id":1037022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1036928#post1036928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noticed that the the rules for Light Weapons don't require you to be rolling on Weaponry</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;These maneuvers may only be used with one-handed weapons with a damage rating of two or less.&quot; So while you don't need the Weaponry skill to be involved in the dice pool, you do need to be using a weapon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1036928#post1036928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so for 7 merit dots (Street Fighting 2, Shive 2, Light Weapons 2 and Martal Arts 1) you can roll Brawl plus your Defence -4 to stake a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thrust trades Defense for extra dice on attack pools, not for damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1036928#post1036928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A strict reading of the rules (but no sane ST) would also allow you to use both Flurry and Whirlwind Strike at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whirlwind Strike and Flurry both provide the same benefit (as long as you have your Defense, any opponent that comes within range automatically takes damage), so as per the 5th restriction in the stacking Maneuvers rules from Hurt Locker, only the higher damage would apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:29:53-08:00","id":1037030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1037022#post1037022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;These maneuvers may only be used with one-handed weapons with a damage rating of two or less.&quot; So while you don't need the Weaponry skill to be involved in the dice pool, you do need to be using a weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were using Shiv 2 to get a light rating 1 weapon, presumably a stake or pencil. It also offers this, 'Your character may use the Brawl Skill to use this weapon.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:46:45-08:00","id":1037034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1037030#post1037030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were using Shiv 2 to get a light rating 1 weapon, presumably a stake or pencil. It also offers this, 'Your character may use the Brawl Skill to use this weapon.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, which would absolutely work. I was just adding that you do need a feature like Shiv or Transfer Maneuver to use a weapon with Brawl instead of Weaponry in order to use Light Weapons Maneuvers with Brawl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T01:46:57-08:00","id":1037084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1036951#post1036951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should be -2, although the attribute prereqs make that a hefty investment just to be able to trade brawl for weaponry on the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed, I was thinking of the need to do 5 damage part of staking. The main benefit of the build is letting you use the two fighting styles together, being able to leave Weaponry at 2 dots unless you want to use a damage 2+ weapon is just the icing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1037022#post1037022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;These maneuvers may only be used with one-handed weapons with a damage rating of two or less.&quot; So while you don't need the Weaponry skill to be involved in the dice pool, you do need to be using a weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that's why Shiv was part of the build.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1037022#post1037022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thrust trades Defense for extra dice on attack pools, not for damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how I gave you the impression I thought Defense was adding to damage, is there something in my wording I should change?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1037022#post1037022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whirlwind Strike and Flurry both provide the same benefit (as long as you have your Defense, any opponent that comes within range automatically takes damage), so as per the 5th restriction in the stacking Maneuvers rules from Hurt Locker, only the higher damage would apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have Hurt Locker but even if you can rule lawyer around that restriction (for example arguing that one does leathal and one does bashing) I agree it shouldn't be allowed.<br /> <br /> I acknolage that this isn't going to be as much use outside of vampire hunting and I'm not sure if I would use it (there are probably better things to spend the four XP needed to dip into Street Fighting and getting Shiv if it's not part of the build you want) but if you're making a Street Fighter who may fight vampires this could be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T04:58:53-08:00","id":1037124,"title":"","content":"Mages, in my opinion, benefit the least from FS. The types of challenges the Awakened face require a greater flexibility than martial arts, especially when combined with facing Praetoreans that can negate Fighting Styles. You're almost better off with focusing on raw skill and attributes with the occasional spell to back up. Focusing on skills also improves your Adamantine Arrow rotes, which is also a nice bonus. I've seen some pick up a dot or two at low levels, but most Arrows seem to be leering away from Fighting Styles in favor of other interests and areas to invest XP in. If they do need to go into melee or ranged combat, they tend to either borrow or cast Kinetic Blow, which seems to work well for them in general as a set up for casting a spell the next round. <br /> <br /> Changelings are currently the only non-Mage splats I'm familiar with that have ways of raising their Dexterity, making them excellent with Fighting Finesse styles, coupled with Street Fighting 1, if they choose to go that route. Qualifies them for shiv as well, letting them have some rather potent tactics under their hands. There's also the Elemental FS, which, despite problems with Cloak of Element's duration, is quite potent when active, giving some powerful bonuses to Defense and damage. Given how changeligns can have crazy high Defense, I've seen investments into Unarmed and Armed Defense as well. Lots of 'lings have also been going with the claw route, which sees a lot of Martial Arts and Street Fighting.<br /> <br /> Vampires... There's a few main routes that I've seen routinely used. Protean claws with Martial Arts or Street and combined with the Frenzy FS. Heavy Weaponry, especially with Vigor. Or vitae lash / chain weapon combined with grappling-to-feeding. Mehket sniper. Yes, guns deal bashing, but with that new set of devotions, there's definite interest. Some of my players are looking into the Crone's new defensive style when combined with Armed / Unarmed Defense. <br /> <br /> Werewolves Iv'e seen fall into Street, Tactical Shifting and Aggressive, as well as a few grappling FS. Grappling and Cheap Shot are often combined with Killing Blow for some powerful combos. <br /> <br /> Demons almost always seem to devolve to guns, in my experience. Marksmanship and Firefight. Yes, some demon forms come with swords, and they're nice swords, better than mundane ones by a little bit. But there's a lack of supporting Embeds / Exploits, so my groups shy away from using things like that. And using modern weapons is just more thematically appropriate for demons to the point that I've never seen it really employed. I've seen only one character invest in Heavy Weapons to use a sword-wielding destroyer, and I can count the number of times it came up on one hand. <br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly, let me touch on the Avoidance Fighting Style. If you have an assassin-themed character, this is a great Fighting Style. Irraka and Darklings, in particular, have seen great use of it, angling it to arrange surprise attacks with alarming frequency. I've seen an Irraka HiD to combining it with Killing Blow. I imagine that GotV would make use of it with fair frequency. Avoidance is a great FS, no matter the game, for sneaky-stabby types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T10:16:24-08:00","id":1037272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1037084#post1037084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how I gave you the impression I thought Defense was adding to damage, is there something in my wording I should change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry. I assumed because you specified the two dot version of Shiv and a -4 penalty on Thrust when talking about staking vampires that you were trying to get the damage modifier up to +5 so you'd be guaranteed to stake in one hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:29:57-08:00","id":1037398,"title":"","content":"Ah no that was me not checking the penalty to target the heart. Still need the 4 success to make it work but as you've got the option of trading in your Defence you should have a decent dice pool.<br /> Fail and the vampire eats you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:07:20-08:00","id":1037434,"title":"","content":"Staking is seriously tough business, it's not like Buffy at all. A werewolf who tore through people like Peg Bundy through bonbons took three turns to stake a vampire and then it only worked because we hammered in a ruling so that the 5 damage could be inflicted over the course of multiple rounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T16:31:04-08:00","id":1037470,"title":"","content":"The best way to get 5 damage is with something like Vigor, pity the kindred with an angry Nosferatu after him.<br /> <br /> On a slightly different note I'm thinking of making a Meket that takes advantage of the Choke Holed merit, any advice on making a grapple fighter? It looks like I need to keep winning the Brawl opposed roll so I need to maximise my dice pool. I may use Martal Arts as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:53:04-08:00","id":1037561,"title":"","content":"As a vamp your best option there is probably Vigor. Very few mortal merits boost the dice pool for grappling. You can take area of expertise for a cheap +2, but almost all grappling merits give you new maneuvers or modify existing ones rather than increasing your pool. The one notable exception is Strength Performance. Goes great with Vigor and will give you an extra success on any successful strength roll.<br /> <br /> Also, trained bite is one dot for an extra +1 lethal to your bite attacks. I would make sure to okay it with your ST, but arguably clinch strike could allow you to grab and bite in a single action even outside of frenzy. Alternatively, the Riding the Wave style allows you to take advantage of frenzy, which gives some impressive buffs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:17:04-08:00","id":1037569,"title":"","content":"Best thing for grapple-vamp is Vigor and Frenzy FS / Coil of Wyrm. Add on a whip or chain weapon for an extra die or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:22:47-08:00","id":1037622,"title":"","content":"Vampires have one thing going for them that no-one here's mentioned:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/pVuMJLde\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Up Fucking Murderer</a><br /> <br /> Screw grapple-vamp - stack up on some nice &quot;sacrifice your Defense&quot; styles and <i>combine that which was not meant to be combined</i>.<br /> <br /> In general, vampire powers tend to synergise <i>really</i> well with Fighting Styles.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> More on topic, Kindred with Improvised Weaponry are <i>terrifying</i>. <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/Ctvypkab\" target=\"_blank\">If You Can't Duck It</a> lets them enhance the Durability and Structure of objects, and Improvised Weaponry's later dots let you spend Structure for cool effects, like <i>bonus damage on all-out attacks</i>.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I like my pencils as +7L light weapons, don't you?<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> Oh, and does anyone have a fixed version of the Light Weapons merit? The third dot doesn't actually have any mechanics - it goes from opening flavor text directly to an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T21:22:02-08:00","id":1037651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1037622#post1037622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and does anyone have a fixed version of the Light Weapons merit? The third dot doesn't actually have any mechanics - it goes from opening flavor text directly to an example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the version in the GMC rules update chapter:<br /> <br /> With a flourish to one direction, your character can distract an opponent for a cleaner, more ef-fective follow-up strike. Make an attack roll as normal, but the attack causes no damage. The next attack your character makes against the same opponent ignores Defense equal to the damage the attack would have caused, and adds the feint\u2019s successes rolled as additional damage if successful. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T02:14:18-08:00","id":1037717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1037622#post1037622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I like my pencils as +7L light weapons, don't you?<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like them more as a +7 heavy weapon so I could spend a Willpower to get 7 armor. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T03:48:54-08:00","id":1037749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1037622#post1037622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More on topic, Kindred with Improvised Weaponry are <i>terrifying</i>. <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/Ctvypkab\" target=\"_blank\">If You Can't Duck It</a> lets them enhance the Durability and Structure of objects, and Improvised Weaponry's later dots let you spend Structure for cool effects, like <i>bonus damage on all-out attacks</i>.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I like my pencils as +7L light weapons, don't you?</div> </div> </div> </div> Combine with Berserker 3. While the rest of Berserker is highly questionable, the third dot lets you use a weapon's Durability as its base weapon bonus. Add on extra Vigor to boost more extra damage....<br /> <br /> If You Can't Duck It takes a turn to invoke, so its a bit iffy in some situations where you need to swap Improvised Weaponry's weapon, but dear gods is it a powerful little bugger when used to the utmost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T04:54:13-08:00","id":1037771,"title":"","content":"Improvised Weaponry gives you ability to pick a weapon as reflexive action, I think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T04:59:41-08:00","id":1037772,"title":"","content":"It does, but still, using a turn to use the devotion on it is kind of difficult after a point. Improvised Weaponry's feature is to grab a weapon, burn through the object's structure, toss it away, then grab a new one. The devotion creates a kind of hiccup in that process, which can be critical in combat.<br /> <br /> Although, don't we have a devotion for speeding up others? Cost 2 vitae each time, but it'll work then. Okay, nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T11:41:51-08:00","id":1037940,"title":"","content":"The thing is that you only get the weapon bonus when you're actually making an all-out attack with the pencil. So the armor is a no-go, I'm afraid.<br /> <br /> Using Improvised Weaponry \u2022\u2022, on the other hand...<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> And good catch on Berserker \u2022\u2022\u2022 - since you're breaking the weapon <i>anyway</i>, the drawback loses its teeth.<br /> <br /> &quot;For 2 vitae 1 wp, turn anything within reach into a one-shot +[Resilience + Vigor + 2]L weapon as a Reflexive action&quot; is a <i>pretty metal combat trick</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:52:54-08:00","id":1038086,"title":"","content":"Making an All Out Attack doesn't deprive you of Armor, actually. Charging your opponent won't make you any less armored or, in case of Warding Stance, won't change the fact that between you and them there is this massive car obstructing the way of your blows. <br /> (Of course, All Out Attack helps your opponent in overriding armor by getting rid of your Defense, and thus making any Called Shot needed to circumvent the Armor easier)<br /> And yeah, I forgot that you need to break the weapon for 3rd dot of ImproWeapon, because I focus way too much on it's second dot. Actually forgot the third one is there!<br /> <br /> Too bad the Berserker combo is so XP intensive...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:20:49-08:00","id":1038118,"title":"","content":"Vampires get it cheaper, since they get free dots of Strength from Vigor!<br /> <br /> Also, the reason I think it wouldn't work with Warding Stance is that my reading of IW3 is that that weapon bonus <i>only</i> applies to that one attack.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> Actually, the full XP costs:<br /> <br /> You can start the trick from character creation as a Daeva - just start with a full Celerity 1/Resilience 1/Vigor 1 spread. If you leave out Berserker for a while, Improvised Weaponry 3 is just three of your merit dots.<br /> <br /> You're 6xp away from starting the tie-clip/high-heel/insert-other-article-of-clothing-here <i>murder</i>. It's less worth it for burst damage at low Resilience/Vigor, but the fact that you can A) deal Lethal to other vampires with your tie-clip and B) you get to add Celerity to all appropriate rolls...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:10:43-08:00","id":1038142,"title":"","content":"Definitely worth it for a Vampire. Especially because the Devotion has out of combat uses due to the ability to increase bonus on intended applications of the item.<br /> Blood soaked dress, for example...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:01:44-08:00","id":1038174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1038142#post1038142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely worth it for a Vampire. Especially because the Devotion has out of combat uses due to the ability to increase bonus on intended applications of the item.<br /> Blood soaked dress, for example...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of the better Devotions, really - sure it's not <i>flashy</i>, but it's so <i>versatile</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:43:44-08:00","id":1038204,"title":"","content":"So, Improved Weaponry with Berserker is a good combo. Anyone else have some interesting combinations with Fighting Styles that they enjoy using?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:01:12-08:00","id":1038217,"title":"","content":"Could you use Keep at Bay to link into Efficient Killer?<br /> <br /> Keep at Bay (\u2022\u2022): Your character can threaten an opponent with her weapon to prevent maneuvering. Choose an opponent with a shorter weapon; if that opponent takes any action other than backing away or Dodging he loses his Defense against your character\u2019s next attack.<br /> <br /> When in Gauru form, any time an opponent is completely denied her Defense \u2014 for example, if she\u2019s sacrificed it for an all-out attack, during a successful ambush, or when activating certain Merits \u2014 you can use Efficient Killer.<br /> <br /> The only problem I see is the 'completely denied her Defense' part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-25-2017, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:02:35-08:00","id":1038219,"title":"","content":"Powered Projectile, which <i>technically</i> works with guns, goes <i>great</i> with Marksmanship.<br /> <br /> Staff Fighting and Spear and Bayonet work together <i>viciously</i> - Medium Autofire attacks with the ability to auto-cause bleeding that <i>isn't</i> a Tilt (for some reason) is <i>boss</i>. It also makes you a defensive <i>beast</i> (or at least it would if this was Exalted - Melee isn't a Skill in this game, devs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Oh, and I want to bring up the fact that any grappling merit you might have works <i>perfectly</i> well with Telekinesis...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 01-25-2017, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:14:40-08:00","id":1038232,"title":"","content":"<u>One Weird Trick to Never Get Jumped by Another Vampire Again! (Sheriffs Hate Him!)</u><br /> <br /> <b>Blood Potency 2+, Natural Born Killer, and Quickdraw (Crossbow).</b> You can't be surprised, you can always have your crossbow at the ready on the first turn of combat, and on the first turn you can stake in one crossbow hit. If your opponent has higher Initiative, you can use Celerity to interrupt.<br /> <b>Optional: Firefight 1, Fast Reflexes up to 3. </b>Increase your Initiative so you have a better chance of going first. If you don't need to spend Vitae to interrupt with Celerity, you can instead spend it on multiplying your speed to launch a surprise attack (somewhat ironic for anyone who thought they'd get the jump on you.)<br /> <b>Optional: Powered Projectile 3, Straight Up Fucking Murderer.</b> Add armor piercing 2 to your crossbow attack to insure a successful staking hit even against most armored opponents. With Murderer, you don't even have to give up your Defense to do it.<br /> <b>Optional: Powered Projectile 4, Quicken Sight.</b> Reduce the penalty for targeting the heart to -1. With Quicken Sight, completely offset the penalty by Aiming <i>(note: text is unclear on what exactly &quot;benefit from aiming instantly&quot; means, so ask your ST before trying this)</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-25-2017, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:28:09-08:00","id":1038245,"title":"","content":"Oh. God.<br /> <br /> 1. Be a Vampire with <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/Upt6BSqc\" target=\"_blank\">Knight Commander</a><br /> 2, Have a thrall with Tactical Telepathy \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> 3. Ghoul them, giving them a dot or two of Celerity.<br /> 4. You have HOW MANY bonus dice on that roll?<br /> <br /> One of the benefits of the higher levels of Tactical Telepathy is that your telepathic &quot;network&quot; can spend Willpower on other people's rolls, which explicitly stacks. One of Knight Commander's benefits is that you can let your Enthralled minions spend one Willpower per turn without actually <i>spending</i> Willpower.<br /> <br /> There's no explicit upward limit on how many targets can be subject to either effect. The only limiting factor of Tactical Telepathy is that you take a -1 penalty to your roll for each person past the first you try to include in your network... which is <i>nothing</i> when you can get such cheap, high bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T01:41:43-08:00","id":1038301,"title":"","content":"Ghouls lose supernatural merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T01:50:45-08:00","id":1038303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1038301#post1038301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls lose supernatural merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think this is dumb (non-major splats should keep them) it is spelled out pretty explicitly in ChroD.<br /> Can Ghouls take the Coil that lets them learn supernatural merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T02:22:34-08:00","id":1038304,"title":"","content":"No coils for ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T03:39:51-08:00","id":1038318,"title":"","content":"It might be posable to make an Auspex devotion that gives you a similar benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T05:14:36-08:00","id":1038347,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Could you use Keep at Bay to link into Efficient Killer?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Umm... what about the &quot;shorter weapon&quot; part? Efficent Killer is a merit that relies on Brawl skill. In other words, the Gauru is killing with their claws and teeth. Keep at Bay requires you to be using a weapon of some size larger than your opponent. Emphasis on the word weapon. The two seem incompatable at heart. </span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> And I'm fairly sure that this particular emphasis will prevent you from using the </span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Transfer Maneuver merit as well, since that merit is banned for merits that require the presence of a weapon. I suppose you could make a fetish that would allow all this to chain, but by default, I would say no.</span></span><br /> <br /> Keep at Bay is admittedly a pretty cheesy way to deny someone their Defense, especially since you can't Dodge if you've already acted in a turn. So, if someone with a shorter weapon goes first, or the Spear FS user holds her action action, then the first person have no way of avoiding a spear attack. Combine with Heavy Weapon and Staff Fighting to deal a heavy blow, then keep a target out of reach while waiting for them to bleed out.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T06:38:00-08:00","id":1038382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1038245#post1038245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. God.<br /> <br /> 1. Be a Vampire with <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/Upt6BSqc\" target=\"_blank\">Knight Commander</a><br /> 2, Have a thrall with Tactical Telepathy \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> 3. Ghoul them, giving them a dot or two of Celerity.<br /> 4. You have HOW MANY bonus dice on that roll?<br /> <br /> One of the benefits of the higher levels of Tactical Telepathy is that your telepathic &quot;network&quot; can spend Willpower on other people's rolls, which explicitly stacks. One of Knight Commander's benefits is that you can let your Enthralled minions spend one Willpower per turn without actually <i>spending</i> Willpower.<br /> <br /> There's no explicit upward limit on how many targets can be subject to either effect. The only limiting factor of Tactical Telepathy is that you take a -1 penalty to your roll for each person past the first you try to include in your network... which is <i>nothing</i> when you can get such cheap, high bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does Celerity factor in on the importance here? It seems like the heavy lifters are Knight Commander (+Enthralled Condition) and Tactical Telepathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:29:59-08:00","id":1038609,"title":"","content":"1) You're a Daeva - get your hands on The Wish. Now they have Celerity.<br /> <br /> 2) Tactical Telepathy 3 lets everyone in the group act at the same initiative count as the telepath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:35:53-08:00","id":1038614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1038347#post1038347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Umm... what about the &quot;shorter weapon&quot; part? Efficent Killer is a merit that relies on Brawl skill. In other words, the Gauru is killing with their claws and teeth. Keep at Bay requires you to be using a weapon of some size larger than your opponent. Emphasis on the word weapon. The two seem incompatable at heart. </span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> And I'm fairly sure that this particular emphasis will prevent you from using the </span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Transfer Maneuver merit as well, since that merit is banned for merits that require the presence of a weapon. I suppose you could make a fetish that would allow all this to chain, but by default, I would say no.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That part doesn't seem like a problem. A werewolf can simply have a large weapon, they're still capable of making bite attacks with Brawl, or even just their other claws. There was a fetish weapon in first edition that was a road sign of some sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T20:36:46-08:00","id":1038739,"title":"","content":"Umm... I'm going to go ahead and say that yes, that is a problem. The whole point of having a larger weapon is so that your'e keeping distance - its right in the name &quot;Keep at Bay.&quot; As in, keep away. If you're biting, you're moving into close distance. The two seem fundamentally incompatable. If you're not using the larger weapon, then you're not using the technique. If you are using the &quot;spear&quot; then you're not biting. You can't both bite and spear in a single attack action.<br /> <br /> If you want an absolute rule that they're incompatable, then I point you to Hurt Locker p. 44. &quot;4. You can\u2019t stack maneuvers that use different dice pools, unless changing the dice pool is a benefit the Merit specifically confers.&quot; One uses Weaponry, the other Brawl. Different dice pools. They are both categorized as Fighting Merits, and the section specifically is refering to any Fighting Merits, not just Fighting Styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-26-2017, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T23:16:25-08:00","id":1038776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1038739#post1038739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't both bite and spear in a single attack action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you of the view that a single attack action is a single blow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T05:28:25-08:00","id":1038839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1038776#post1038776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you of the view that a single attack action is a single blow?</div> </div> </div> </div> No. I'm of the view that you can't use both a Weaponry and a Brawl technique in the same attack action*. While you can make as many attacks as you want during the attack action, there's are strict mechanical differences between using a sword, a knife, a gun and/or your body when making an attack.<br /> <br /> The above view is supported by the Style Tags rules, as put forwards on Hurt Locker p44, and should apply to all Styles drawn from that book. Tags with &quot;Creature&quot; and &quot;Pole Arm&quot; styles are distinct and don't really mix. Now, I would accept an argument for mixing Street Fighting and Efficent Killer, and maybe Martial Arts. Both those are core book (thus pre-Tag) and I think meant to apply to claw-users, notably Gangrel, and I've never heard that you can't use Cheap Shot with Gauru. I think that claws + Street is working as intended. But &quot;Pole Arms&quot; shouldn't work with &quot;Striking&quot; or &quot;Creature&quot; styles anymore than it should work with &quot;Archery&quot; styles. <br /> <br /> I am also of the view that story should matter here (also supported by p44 of Hurt Locker). Techniques are more than a collection of dry numbers. They're telling a story of how the character is acting and moving. Now, while there is flexibility to story, there's also a point where two stories tell very different things that are contradictory - you can't both be keep a length of distance AND be within hugging distance. The descriptions are clashing. This is definitely a consideration that needs to be made - Hurt Locker makes that clear enough - but the judgement on that is subjective enough that I'm not relying on it to make my argument, instead relying on different rules. However, story alone is a strong enough argument that you can't say a certain maneuver should be allowed (or disallowed, if I'm being fair) by the default rules. Don't rely on such working without ST approval, and if the ST says no, its entirely justified.<br /> <br /> * While there are some merits and techniques that do mix brawl and weaponry, as far as I know there are no such merits for mixing Gauru bites and spear use. And without a merit, you don't get the mechanical benefits of mixing brawl and weaponry techniques. So, while there are exceptions, they have to be purchased with xp somehow, usually in merit form. Again, refer to p44 of Hurt Locker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T05:54:57-08:00","id":1038848,"title":"","content":"Efficient killer doesn't actually require using your teeth or claws.<br /> Can Gauru even use weapons?<br /> <br /> (Obviously it's totally reasonable to require using Teeth/Claws for Efficient Killer, given that it requires Brawl and the text mentions 'clamping down', but it's not <i>actually</i> an explicit requirement)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T05:58:04-08:00","id":1038849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1038848#post1038848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Gauru even use weapons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they can..<br /> <br /> Still she's got a point. Seems like a better way to pull it off would be to just turn off the lights, inflicting the Blinded Tilt, providing they can't see in the dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-27-2017, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T06:05:50-08:00","id":1038854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1038849#post1038849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes they can..<br /> <br /> Still she's got a point. Seems like a better way to pull it off would be to just turn off the lights, inflicting the Blinded Tilt, providing they can't see in the dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I just think it's important to talk about what the rules actually say as well as the best interpretation and table preference.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't let them work, for all of the same reasons MCN mentioned. Doesn't mean we shouldn't talk about the mechanics as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T07:59:32-08:00","id":1038897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1038848#post1038848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Efficient killer doesn't actually require using your teeth or claws.</div> </div> </div> </div> Claws are immaterial; brawl skill is the deciding factor in my argument. I brought up claws in my last post only in relationship to Gangrel claw users.<br /> <br /> Claws (and teeth) are only relevant in deciding which of the Brawl-based Fighting Merits Gauru qualifies for. As I mentioned above, I would say that the Street merits can be used, and I could see arguments for Unarmed Defensive and maybe some of the Martial Arts, but that last one is questionable. You can use Grappling merits, but I would not allow Boxing with claws. I suppose you could argue that Gauru closes their claws and boxes or kung fu like normal, but I'm not interested in exploring that situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T11:57:28-08:00","id":1039026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1038897#post1038897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Claws are immaterial; brawl skill is the deciding factor in my argument. I brought up claws in my last post only in relationship to Gangrel claw users.<br /> <br /> Claws (and teeth) are only relevant in deciding which of the Brawl-based Fighting Merits Gauru qualifies for. As I mentioned above, I would say that the Street merits can be used, and I could see arguments for Unarmed Defensive and maybe some of the Martial Arts, but that last one is questionable. You can use Grappling merits, but I would not allow Boxing with claws. I suppose you could argue that Gauru closes their claws and boxes or kung fu like normal, but I'm not interested in exploring that situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, given the way Atavisms manifest their effects in the physical world, it seems all maneuvers of Boxing, Grappling, Martial Arts, Relentless Assault, and Street Fighting can be normally used by Beasts, unless the Horror is somehow physically manifest (e.g. in the Lair, or an Incarnate Adopting the Beast-Shape). As a matter of fact, many of these Styles' maneuvers can synergize rather well with most combat Atavisms and advanced Merits (Double Jointed, Iron Skin, Killer Instinct).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-27-2017, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T09:20:55-08:00","id":1039454,"title":"","content":"You could probably get a Fetish that would let you use Efficient Killer with a spear - it feels like a sufficiently &quot;primal&quot; weapon that it scans well mentally, and Fetishes <i>are</i> supposed to expand your capabilities in sideways ways...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:03:40-08:00","id":1040425,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts 5 turns your unarmed attacks into 2L weapons(basically). Protean 4 says it adds +2 lethal weapon modifier to all brawl attacks&quot;. Do those two things stack, or are they redundant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:09:54-08:00","id":1040430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade10</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040425#post1040425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts 5 turns your unarmed attacks into 2L weapons(basically). Protean 4 says it adds +2 lethal weapon modifier to all brawl attacks&quot;. Do those two things stack, or are they redundant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say redundant, because Protean works by swapping out your Martial Arts-enhanced fists with claws or some similar appendages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:36:51-08:00","id":1040439,"title":"","content":"Is fists always expected? All it ever says, that I saw, in the mechanics was &quot;unarmed&quot;, and plenty of martial arts go beyond simple kicks and punches. Clawing is a part of several martial art styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:45:45-08:00","id":1040444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade10</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040439#post1040439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is fists always expected? All it ever says, that I saw, in the mechanics was &quot;unarmed&quot;, and plenty of martial arts go beyond simple kicks and punches. Clawing is a part of several martial art styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just fists - the point is that the human limb you have enhanced with martial arts training is being replaced by a non-human limb that can be used in combat immediately without training.<br /> <br /> So yes, you can train to make your own claws a viable weapon. But the moment you activate Protean, all that toughened fingers and claws are gone and replaced with something else. How could someone benefit from his human fingers and claws at that point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T23:12:29-08:00","id":1040455,"title":"","content":"Because the principle is still, ultimately, the same. It's minor differences at most, you are still clawing at something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:16:50-08:00","id":1040522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade10</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040455#post1040455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the principle is still, ultimately, the same. It's minor differences at most, you are still clawing at something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly doubt that martial arts schools train their students in how to fight with the hands and arms of a bear, tiger, dragon, or some tentacled monstrosity that Protean 4 allows you to transform into, despite how awesome that sounds now that I've typed it.<br /> <br /> If someone managed to practice how to fight effectively with the claws of a monster, then sure. But that sounds more like a different Fighting Style that's intended for people who can do such things, rather than Martial Arts, which is meant for humans and assumes its practitioners have human anatomy and will use human hands to execute its moves.<br /> <br /> Hmm... was there a Fighting Style for vampires that use Protean? That sounds like a good niche to homebrew a Merit into.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:53:39-08:00","id":1040539,"title":"","content":"Narratively, human martial arts probably aren't helping you wield clawed appendages, or stranger things.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, a good way to represent learning how to fight similarly with enhanced limbs is to just allow the merit to be used with enhanced limbs. There's no need to build new ones from the ground up, just reflavor the existing ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:49:09-08:00","id":1040561,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to repost the same thing I said in the VtR thread.<br /> <br /> Its always been a thing in the nWoD that claws are incompatable with human Fighting Styles. Its clear that standard holds true for the CofD as well, but with a slightly less restrictions. Only the three (four if you count the alternate Martial Arts techniques) &quot;Striking&quot; styles are incompatable now, instead of huge swaths of techniques. Martial Arts, Unarmed Defense and Boxing are all banned from use with claws.<br /> <br /> The &quot;claws can work with human techniques&quot; arguement is pretty old by this point; if you want to allow it at your table, go ahead. Its going to be a house rule, however, since official rules disallow it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040522#post1040522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... was there a Fighting Style for vampires that use Protean? That sounds like a good niche to homebrew a Merit into.</div> </div> </div> </div> While you can't use Striking or the various Weaponry-based techniques, that does leave Temple Guardian, Tactical-based Styles (especially Street Fighting), and there's always Grappling. Relentless Assault (BtP version) works well. Berserk technically works, but that's a questionable FS. You can use Parkour, Strength Performance and Systema, though I don't think those involve attacking.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, while we're on the subject of Parkour.... I'm not sure how that would be used in combat. I've heard of using Freeflow to bounce into combat, attack, and then run away out of melee distance. Is that possible? Actually, do you have to do a move-then-instant attack? Can you move in, hit, then move back out with your movement? I don't see anything that says that you can't move both before and after your allotted Instant Action. And how does Freeflow work with the meditation requirement? Is that right before the scene, or at the beginning of the day, or...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-30-2017, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:04:35-08:00","id":1040567,"title":"","content":"Lack of stacking makes Martial Arts 4/5 a good replacement of Protean 2/4 (quite possibly enhanced by Claws of the Unholy) for vampires who lack the Discipline or want to spare the Vitae, and redundant otherwise. It works pretty much the same way for Beasts: Martial Arts 4/5 acts as a replacement of the Low Satiety variants of Cyclopean Strength, Limb from Limb, or Monster from the Deep for characters who lack these Atavisms or don't care being at Low Satiety at the moment, or most of the time. Otherwise it is redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-30-2017, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:54:21-08:00","id":1040596,"title":"","content":"Cyclopean strength adds automatic successes on strength rolls when you expend satiety, which is distinct from a weapon modifier.<br /> <br /> Also, while I agree the weapon modifier from Martial Arts 5 doesn't stack with Protean, Limb from Limb, etc, I don't see the argument for disallowing claws to make use of any striking style maneuver. I have claws instead of fists so I can't use Unarmed Defense to trip people??? The five points from Hurt Locker are a better way of determining case by case what stacks and what doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:00:15-08:00","id":1040604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040596#post1040596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cyclopean strength adds automatic successes on strength rolls when you expend satiety, which is distinct from a weapon modifier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of the Low Satiety variant, which applies to thrown or improvised weapons.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:08:58-08:00","id":1040606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040596#post1040596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't see the argument for disallowing claws to make use of any striking style maneuver.</div> </div> </div> </div> From Hurt Locker, but page 45 this time! <br /> <br /> &quot;Striking: The focus is on striking with fists, feet, elbows, knees, and other human \u201cnatural weapons.\u201d Inhuman natural weapons are the province of Creature styles. Striking may function with weapons that utilize the Brawl Skill. Styles: Boxing, Martial Arts, Unarmed Defense&quot; <br /> <br /> As well, under Creature, we have this: &quot;Default Keywords are: Avian, Bite, Claw, and Constrictor.&quot;<br /> <br /> Its not so much an argument as taking directly from the book. Claws are an inhuman natural weapon to the point they're even listed under &quot;Creature.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The five points from Hurt Locker are a better way of determining case by case what stacks and what doesn't. </div> </div> </div> Good thing this falls under point 2, then. &quot;The required equipment or other circumstances for all maneuvers used must be present.&quot; In this case, if you're attacking with claws, you're not attacking using the human natural weaponry that Striking Styles require.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:32:56-08:00","id":1040621,"title":"","content":"Again, claiming that replacing normal human hands with claws prevents you from using the ability makes zero sense when applied to numerous maneuvers from those styles. Tripping somebody with unarmed defense isn't using your claws, it's using your legs. &quot;Bobbing, weaving and angling away from blows&quot; is not impacted by having claws. <br /> <br /> It should be patently obvious that a Gangrel, Beast, etc can learn striking styles for when they don't have their supernatural powers active since they have normal human hands at that point. Activating said powers should in no way prevent them from using such maneuvers as don't involve their claws. I don't forget how to duck or trip people because my bare hands are now bear hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T09:28:38-08:00","id":1040711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040621#post1040621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, claiming that replacing normal human hands with claws prevents you from using the ability makes zero sense when applied to numerous maneuvers from those styles. Tripping somebody with unarmed defense isn't using your claws, it's using your legs. &quot;Bobbing, weaving and angling away from blows&quot; is not impacted by having claws.<br /> <br /> It should be patently obvious that a Gangrel, Beast, etc can learn striking styles for when they don't have their supernatural powers active since they have normal human hands at that point. Activating said powers should in no way prevent them from using such maneuvers as don't involve their claws. I don't forget how to duck or trip people because my bare hands are now bear hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're using your feet etc for the manuever it would still work fine, those are listed as compatible 'equipment' for the maneuver. You just don't get to use your claws (and benefit from their bonuses).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T10:34:12-08:00","id":1040753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040561#post1040561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, do you have to do a move-then-instant attack? Can you move in, hit, then move back out with your movement? I don't see anything that says that you can't move both before and after your allotted Instant Action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T10:37:40-08:00","id":1040755,"title":"","content":"Has anyone found any of the 'worst fighting styles'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T10:46:11-08:00","id":1040763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040755#post1040755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone found any of the 'worst fighting styles'?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the discussion so far - Striking styles if you're a claw maniac are literally just wasted XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:05:00-08:00","id":1040773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040763#post1040763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the discussion so far - Striking styles if you're a claw maniac are literally just wasted XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems poorly thought out. But more likely you could just have a variant of existing fighting styles that allows for use of claws or tentacles or whatever. The book, and even that section, do suggest developing your own Fighting Styles to fit within the Style Tags options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-30-2017, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:53:19-08:00","id":1040919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040621#post1040621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, claiming that replacing normal human hands with claws prevents you from using the ability makes zero sense when applied to numerous maneuvers from those styles. Tripping somebody with unarmed defense isn't using your claws, it's using your legs. &quot;Bobbing, weaving and angling away from blows&quot; is not impacted by having claws.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, as someone else said, you can use them while having claws, you just can't make attacks and deal damage using the claws at the same time. You're not cutting people with claws when attacking with your normal human limbs. I don't forget how to use Heavy Weapon techniques when I'm only carrying around a knife either, but that doesn't mean I can use them.<br /> <br /> The rule seems pretty clear. You don't want to use the rule, sure. There's no badwrongfun police. But its still the default rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Has anyone found any of the 'worst fighting styles'?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> I'm going to go with Berserker. While there's a good combination with Improvised Weaponry at the third dot, the other two levels are generally regarded as crap, and that combo is the only way I've found to make use of any of Berserker.<br /> <br /> Kindred Dueling gets a lot of flak in my ciricles; people buy up to the third dot, and use only that dot and no other. And, even then that's often ignored if there's access to stakes, claws or a blood whip. Or just outright grappling. Or discipline use. Or.. you know, I think you get the idea. <br /> <br /> Close Quarters Combat seems to get a lot of aversion as well. Now, this could be the result of our playstyle, but the first three dots generally end up as dead levels. They seem cool, but I've rarely said that cover was outside of someone's range to reach, rarely seen someone willingly end a grapple when they could control the person for more advantage, and non-magical armor is rare enough that its not relevant. The last two dots sound nice, but then none of my players were interested in reaching that high when they could invest in other, more relevant Styles.<br /> <br /> Light Weapon also gets a lot of grief from my group. The first two dots are, on average, actually detriments than advatnages. Feint, the third dot, seems pretty good if not for the fact that Cheap Shot is generally considered better, though more expensive. Fourth dot seems solid. Fifth dot... sacrifices your defense in exchange for an extra point of agg. Doing so negates half the earlier levels of the FS, including the extra damage from the fourth dot, actually leading to a net loss of damage output/recieved.<br /> <br /> Chain Weapons is pretty much frowned on. First dot considered too weak, second too situational.<br /> <br /> Throwing is missing the tilt, something rather critical to the FS as a whole. In either case, only two levels and no synergy with anything else, plus throwing has to compete with guns AND has to worry about Defense. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1040763#post1040763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the discussion so far - Striking styles if you're a claw maniac are literally just wasted XP.</div> </div> </div> </div> Claws with Street Fighting is pretty badass. I highly recommend that. Relentless Assault also works wonders with claws, and was originally designed for werewolves in their various forms. Grappling still works, and you can ask your ST if claws count as a grapple aid, like a chain would. As I was wondering above, how the ST handles movement in combat could lend a LOT of power to movement Styles, which includes Parkour and Systema. You could try learning Berserker, but, well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T16:03:53-08:00","id":1040961,"title":"","content":"People don't like Thrust? It's a flat better alternative to All Out Attack (which is admittedly not a terribly high bar). Assuming your ST allows it Thrust combines great with Relentless Assault 2.<br /> <br /> Turnabout is nuts, but yeah I never see anybody take CQC. At least now you can take Systema in place of the first three dots, and the prereqs line up fairly close.<br /> <br /> The fifth dot of Armed Defense is pretty bad. The entire style is weaponry based, so why does it have you making a brawl attack? The third dot is similar but uses weaponry and can hit multiple opponents in a turn.<br /> <br /> Unarmed Defense has two good maneuvers, 3 and 5. The other three aren't great. <br /> <br /> Heavy Weapons 1 is at best situationally useful, and Relentless Assault has a very similar maneuver except that one is -1/+1 instead of -3/+1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:36:50-08:00","id":1041283,"title":"","content":"Relentless Assault and Brute Force work together famously - we're talking 2/3 Armor on any turn where you perform an all-out attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:16:32-08:00","id":1041837,"title":"","content":"Where's brute force? I don't see one in my books...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:52:45-08:00","id":1041855,"title":"","content":"Brute Force is the Promethean core style. The first dot is an incredible swap for Relentless Assault 1, but I don't think the armor from BF 5 stacks with RA 4. Generally when two style merits provide the same type of bonus you get the better of the two, not both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:51:03-08:00","id":1042090,"title":"","content":"Brute Force does explicitly state that the armor stacks...<br /> <br /> But it probably doesn't. Still, yeah, it's a <i>marvellous</i> swap","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:21:53-08:00","id":1042106,"title":"","content":"It's &quot;cumulative with any armor she wears&quot; and while it doesn't specify armor from refinements I would assume it stacks with that as well. My feeling is that armor stacks if it's from different sources, like supernatural armor stacking with worn armor, but just like you can't benefit from wearing a kevlar vest under riot gear gaining two instances of armor from an all out attack wouldn't work.<br /> <br /> What I'm really trying to figure out is what could replace RA 4 if you wanted to do BF1/RA2/RA3/??/BF5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:42:25-08:00","id":1042311,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, armor stacks as long as it all comes from different sources. So, worn armor is one source. Magical armor is a second. Merits that reflect shrugging off damage is a third.<br /> <br /> Transmutations seem to create armor in the form of pliable skin and magnetic fields. This seems to stack with worn armor, given the precidence in other gamelines. I don't think that they stack with each other, however, despite being thematically different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">What I'm really trying to figure out is what could replace RA 4 if you wanted to do BF1/RA2/RA3/??/BF5</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Why not stay with Relentless Assault 4? 1 point of general armor that stacks with everything is always good. <br /> <br /> I'm fairly sure that Brute Force 4, however, does nothing. -2 to target an arm or leg is already standard, and beating Stamina causes the tilt, and that's exactly what BF 4 is claiming to do. Its pretty much reprinting how to cause the Tilts in the first place. </span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-02-2017, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T04:05:14-08:00","id":1042337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1033613-best-and-worst-fighting-styles-for-supernatural-splats?p=1042311#post1042311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly sure that Brute Force 4, however, does nothing. -2 to target an arm or leg is already standard, and beating Stamina causes the tilt, and that's exactly what BF 4 is claiming to do. Its pretty much reprinting how to cause the Tilts in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nearly nothing. It does an extra point of lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T07:01:43-08:00","id":1042389,"title":"","content":"Ah, I missed that. So it does. Very wordy for, &quot;Whenever you inflict an Arm or Leg Wrack Tilt via All Out Attack, deal an extra lethal.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:51:16-08:00","id":1043617,"title":"","content":"Does anybody have favorite hybrid styles? There are so many styles out there but a lot 